<header><p class="muted">NATHAN AI / ONE / PUBLIC-SOURCE RESEARCH</p><h1>Jeffrey Epstein Files — Investigative Archive</h1><p>Creator/research organizer: John “Nathan” Tabor · Compiled November 2, 2026</p><p>Original owner-authored theories and historical mapping threads remain identified as <b>hypotheses</b>. Public documents, reporting, allegations and confirmed judicial findings are separate categories. No named person's appearance in a document proves a crime.</p></header>
<main>
<section class="card"><h2>Historical connection map — author's research path</h2><div class="map"><span class="node">Ancient Rome <small>historical comparison</small></span><span class="divider">→</span><span class="node">Vatican <small>author's institutional-power hypothesis</small></span><span class="divider">→</span><span class="node">Kremlin <small>author's proposed link</small></span><span class="divider">→</span><span class="node">Epstein network <small>separate modern criminal record</small></span><span class="divider">→</span><span class="node">Trump-related files <small>documents & disputed claims</small></span></div><p><b>Interpretation:</b> Arrows represent the owner's questions and proposed connections, <b>not established trafficking routes, proven causation or substantiated accusations</b>. An authenticated evidence chain joining these nodes has not been established by the sources indexed here.</p></section>
<section><h2>Source / claim ledger</h2><label for="q">Search records</label> <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search Trump, Rome, flight logs…" aria-label="Search records"> <label for="type">Type</label> <select id="type"><option value="">All categories</option><option>Primary source</option><option>Reporting</option><option>Author research</option></select><div id="results" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Preservation and evidence rules</h2><p>Keep authored wording unchanged in original-source files when originals are supplied. This public repository includes an indexed recovery summary, not reconstructed verbatim transcripts. Record document IDs, dates, source URLs, page numbers, image hashes, and supporting/contradictory evidence. Do not include victims' identifying details, graphic abuse imagery, private addresses, login credentials, or unpublished evidence in this public site. Counts of name matches are not counts of crimes or victims.</p></section>
</main><footer>Sources link to original publishers. This archive has not ingested the full DOJ multi-million-page corpus and does not claim to contain private FBI or Secret Service files.</footer>
<script>
const records=[
{title:"DOJ Epstein Library",type:"Primary source",date:"2026-09-11 site update",summary:"Official searchable release hub; search and OCR may be incomplete.",url:"https://www.justice.gov/epstein"},
